       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it, but 1000 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any clinical situation where it would be appropriate, and you haven't given a rationale. The harm could be serious and hard to reverse, so I'd rather not put it into the system on a bare confirmation.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you intend an above-label dose,** please talk to pharmacy or the attending about it first. I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale and who approved it. I'd want that approval before I do.\n- **If you're treating an overdose or something else unusual,** that needs toxicology or poison control input (1-800-222-1222 in the US), not a standing daily order.\n\nTell me which of these applies, and I'll help from there."
      }
